ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-94): large blurs at a reduced resolution, as Skia blurs
Library: resvg 0.48.1
Fixes: none (speed: a blur's cost grows with its sigma in pixels, and so with the zoom)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to linebender/resvg (ours)
Remove when: a resvg release blurs large sigmas at a reduced resolution, or this patch no longer applies

A blur whose sigma passes 4 pixels is computed on a copy reduced 2^n times on that axis, with a sigma
of at most 4 there, and enlarged back with bilinear interpolation (filter::blur()); a lone such blur of
the whole region, on a group with no clip path or mask, draws the group itself on the reduced layer,
enlarged within the filter region at full resolution (filter::reduction(), render::render_reduced()).
Each reduced pixel is the mean of the 2^n pixels it covers on a grid that starts at the whole filter
region's origin (outside the region: transparent), and a layer drawn in part starts on that grid, so
that a part of a document drawn alone (a band, a zoom's detail; imageviewer-filter-area.patch) has the
whole's pixels; filter::reach() counts the reduced pixels and the interpolation (blur_reach()). The
owner's artwork: 1.88 levels from Chromium on average (1.75 exact); resvg's reference tests: 74 of
1,730 differ, the blurs by at most 20 levels, 3.1 on average over the pixels that differ by more than
one. Requires imageviewer-filter-area.patch and imageviewer-turbulence-cache.patch (their Context and
reach).

